CRM Recruitment System

This project is a Recruitment CRM designed to help teams manage candidates throughout the hiring process. Built with React (frontend), Node.js + Express (backend), and PostgreSQL (database), it simplifies the workflow from application intake to hiring decisions.

Architecture:   
•	Frontend: React SPA (CRA or Vite) communicating with the API via JSON over HTTPS.
•	Backend: Node.js + Express providing RESTful JSON APIs and handling authentication, business logic, validation, and DB access.
•	Database: PostgreSQL with logical separation of tables for users, candidates, pipeline stages, calls, shortlist, feedback, and activity log.

 Features
•	User Management
o	Secure authentication (email + password).
•	Candidate Management
o	Store and update candidate profiles.
o	Upload & manage resumes (with metadata).
•	Pipeline Tracking
o	Record candidate stages (Applied → Screening → Interview → Offer → Hired).
o	View history of stage changes with timestamps.
•	Call Logs
o	Record recruiter–candidate calls with duration, outcome, and next steps.
•	Feedback System
o	Collect recruiter evaluations (positive/negative/neutral sentiment).
o	Add free-text notes for qualitative input.

               Recruitment Statistics & Insights
•	Applications Overview → Track how many candidates have applied overall.
•	Pipeline Metrics → Count of candidates per stage (Applied, Shortlisted, Rejected, Hired).
•	Conversion Rates → See what percentage of applicants progress from Applied → Shortlisted → Hired.
•	Candidate Sources → Breakdown of applicants by origin (job board, referral, direct website, etc.).
 
How the website works:
1-	Sign in with email + password
2-	Add a new candidate through the dashboard, fill the required fields (name, email, phone number, their CV, and any notes). When the profile is created, the candidate starts at the applied stage.
3-	Move a candidate through the pipeline (applied, screening, interview, offer, hired (or rejected), and can add notes through the process that will be submitted under their name.   
4-	Through the process, candidates are interviewed or called, and they add feedback and a timeline.
